From d15874fc238520fca57b9a697c4f0fd5b249f7b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ademir Terin Junior <juniorterin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:12:50 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] outputs: publish game state (recoil, ammo, life, wins,
 credits) from work RAM

The cabinet outputs carry the lamp latch and the drive board, which is all a
driving cabinet has to say. A Model 2 gun cabinet has no recoil, so nothing
on the board says that a shot was fired or a life lost, and a recoil gun
driven by MAMEHooker or Hook Of The Reaper stays still.

games.xml can now list outputs of a title's own, read from the program's
work RAM once a frame:

  <lamp>   one bit of the lamp latch under another name
  <value>  a number at an address (u8/u16/s16/u32/float), with optional
           <when> conditions for variables that only mean something while a
           player is in the game
  <flag>   1 while a value is above zero
  <pulse>  1 for a few frames each time a value falls or rises

Virtua Cop, Virtua Cop 2, The House of the Dead, Gunblade NY, Behind Enemy
Lines and Rail Chase 2 publish theirs under the names DemulShooter
established for these games (P1_CtmRecoil, P1_Ammo, P1_Clip, P1_Life,
P1_Damaged, P1_LmpStart, P1_GunMotor, Credits), so the stock game files of
those tools work unchanged. The addresses are DemulShooter's where the
revision is the same one; The House of the Dead's are 0x680 further on in
this revision.

The fighting games (Virtua Fighter 2, Fighting Vipers, Sonic the Fighters,
Last Bronx, Dead or Alive revision A) publish P1_Wins and P2_Wins, the
rounds each side has taken in the match being fought, for a scoreboard.
Those were found with two scripted two-player matches, one where only
player 1 attacks and one where only player 2 does: the bytes that step at
each round of the first and stay at zero through the second, and the
reverse.

Twenty-one sets publish Credits. The counter was found by dropping coins
and looking for the byte that counts them, then checked against both coin
chutes and a start. Sets on two coins a credit that start by themselves
when the credit completes (Daytona USA, Sega Rally, Sega Touring Car, Motor
Raid and others) have none: the credit is spent the moment it exists.

The addresses belong to the set that was run, so three of them sit on the
revision a merged archive resolves to (doaa, pltkidsa, zeroguna).

Each was checked with a reader on port 8000 through a scripted game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
